# Feature Documentation Maintenance

For every code change, find the repository feature inventory (`FEATURES.md` or
`feature.md`, case-insensitive) before finalizing the work.

- Update it when the change adds, removes, alters, fixes, or materially changes a user-visible
  feature, workflow, API contract, configuration option, or operational behavior.
- Include the current behavior, affected UI/API surface, relevant configuration, and verification
  status; remove stale counts or claims rather than presenting them as live facts.
- If no feature inventory exists, create `FEATURES.md` at the repository root and document the
  changed capability there.
- Before committing, verify the documentation matches the implementation. Do not defer this step
  to a follow-up task.
